# Build-context hygiene (P0-T5): keep the image small and secrets/data out
# of the build context. Runtime state (app_data, app_assets, static/img,
# custom_libs) reaches the container via bind mounts / vendored code — not
# via COPY of these files.
#
# CRITICAL: custom_libs/ is the vendored markdown library loaded via sys.path
# at runtime — it is deliberately NOT ignored here. Never add it below.

# Virtualenv, VCS, editor, workspace noise
venv/
.git/
.agents/
.vscode/
KANBAN.json
README_Images/

# Runtime data / secrets (bind-mounted or injected at runtime instead)
app_data/
.env

# Python + log junk
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
main.log

# Binary artifacts and one-off dev scripts. The legacy root test_*.py
# scratch scripts are named individually (NOT blanket-ignored) because the
# pytest suite itself lives in tests/ and MUST ship in the image.
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.xlsb
pricing.db
success.pdf
download_pdf*.py
measure_pdf*.py
test_dests.py
test_dests2.py
test_pdf_flask.py
test_weasy.py

# Same junk nested in subpackages (plain `*.pyc` etc. only match the root)
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.log

# The pytest suite + golden PDF baselines ship in the image so the suite can
# run with one command (docker compose run --rm app pytest). Negations come
# last on purpose: later rules override earlier ones, so this also un-ignores
# tests/golden/baselines/*.pdf matched by `*.pdf` above.
!tests/
!tests/**
